#subtitle: Working hours, safety regulations, and the Poorman's Pension.

= Labor Rights

With control of the Labor Ministry, we can set national standards for labor. Our supporters expect us to enforce a 40-hour work week and enforce safety regulations, as well as fully fund the Poorman's Pension program.

# enforce a 40-hour work week
# develop and enforce safety regulations in mines and industries
# works councils are part of another card...

@labor_rights_menu

- @working_hours: Enforce the 40-hour work week.
- @shorten_hours: Shorten work hours less than 40 hours.
- @safety: Develop and enforce safety regulations.
- @unemployment_insurance: Fund the Poorman's Pension program.
- @root: Do not enact any policies.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@working_hours
view-if: working_hours < 2
on-arrival: working_hours += 1; labor_dissent -= 8; left_dissent -= 5; labor_strength += 5; commons_marcher += 7*(1-dissent); gold_relation -= 4; ddp_relation -= 2; lvp_relation -= 3; coalition_dissent += 1; capital_strike_progress += 1 if (gold_relation <= 30 and not lvp_formed); capital_strike_progress += 1 if (lvp_relation <= 30 and lvp_formed); labor_goal_completed = 1; inflation += 0.1; gold_right += 1; ddp_left += 1; ddp_cohesion -= 0.5; lvp_right += 1; labor_goal_marcher += 1; pro_labor += 1; economic_growth -= 0.1

While a 40-hour work week was declared during the Commonwealth Revolution in 4283, enforcement has become increasingly porous over the years. The capitalists have successfully added numerous exceptions and loopholes, returning to the old regime of forced overtime for workers.

Now, with the force of the Labor Ministry, we are finally enforcing the rights of workers to their own time. The Burghers and their political representatives are displeased.

@shorten_hours
view-if: working_hours >= 2 and veran_crash_seen = 1
subtitle: Could we induce more hiring and reduce unemployment by reducing work hours?
on-arrival: working_hours += 1; labor_dissent -= 8; left_dissent -= 5; labor_strength += 5; commons_marcher += 7*(1-dissent); gold_relation -= 4; ddp_relation -= 3; lvp_relation -= 4; coalition_dissent += 1; capital_strike_progress += 1; labor_goal_completed = 1; disfavored -= 0.3; gold_right += 2; ddp_right += 1; ddp_cohesion -= 0.5; lvp_right += 2; labor_goal_marcher += 1; goal_marcher_cancel_peoples += 1; pro_labor += 1; economic_growth -= 0.2;

Some in the labor movement argue that by reducing the maximum number of hours worked, employers would be induced to hire more workers, reducing unemployment. The argument also goes that this would be complementary to deflation, maintaining the same purchasing power for workers by cutting hours without cutting wages. Employers, however, resist this policy, arguing for more flexibility in hiring and firing.

@safety
on-arrival: commons_safety += 1; labor_dissent -= 5; labor_strength += 2; commons_marcher += 5*(1-dissent); capital_strike_progress += 1 if commons_safety >= 3; ddp_right += 1 if commons_safety >= 3; gold_right += 1 if commons_safety >= 3; lvp_right += 1 if commons_safety >= 3; labor_goal_marcher += 1

The Labor Ministry works on developing and enforcing safety regulations, in order to ensure healty working conditions for the proletariat. [? if commons_safety >= 3 : Businesses have begun to argue that our focus on safety is overbearing and unnecessary, interfering with the economy. ?]

@unemployment_insurance
view-if: disfavored >= unemployment_insurance_threshold + 4
subtitle: With increasing unemployment, we must find new ways to fund our signature program.

With the onset of the economic calamity and its throngs of unemployed, our the Poorman's Pension program is under strain. The program was never designed for this many claimants; something must be done to balance the budget.

- @cut_benefits: Cut benefits.
- @increase_employers: Increase employer contributions.
- @balance: Increase both employer and employee contributions.
- @labor_rights_menu: We can defer this decision for now.

@cut_benefits
subtitle: The workers will regard this as a betrayal.
on-arrival: commons_marcher -= 0.12*commons_marcher; disfavored_marcher -= 0.2*disfavored_marcher; commons_collectivist += 5; commons_royalist += 5; disfavored_collectivist += 5; disfavored_royalist += 5; left_dissent += 15; center_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 15; reformist_dissent += 5; welfare -= 2; budget += 1; disfavored += 3; pro_republic -= 4; collectivist_relation -= 8; inflation -= 2; unemployment_insurance_threshold = disfavored; unemployment_insurance_timer = 10; gold_left += 2; ddp_left += 2 if ddp_ideology == "Left"; commons_ddp += 3 if ddp_ideology == "Left"; lvp_left += 1; goal_marcher_cancel += 1; labor_goal_marcher_peoples += 1; economic_growth -= 0.2;

For budgetary reasons, we have cut the Poorman's Pension benefits. Unfortunately, our reasons for fiscal discipline are alien to the workers. They are furious at our betrayal, as are a good portion of our membership throughout the factions. Our loss is the <span style="color: #700000 ;">**Collectivists**</span>'s gain, and even the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>, those lapdogs of the Burghers, have joined in criticizing us for our austerity.

@increase_employers
subtitle: Employers are strongly against this. [? if in_grand_coalition: The [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?] will likely break the coalition. ?][? if in_weimar_coalition and lvp_formed: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> will likely break the coalition. ?]
on-arrival: capital_strike_progress += 2; coalition_dissent = 2 if in_grand_coalition; coalition_dissent = 2 if (in_weimar_coalition and lvp_formed); coalition_dissent += 1; coalition_dissent += 1 if (lvp_ideology == "Right" and in_weimar_coalition and lvp_formed); welfare += 1; commons_marcher += 6*(1-dissent); disfavored_marcher += 6*(1-dissent); guild_marcher -= 6*(1-dissent); burgher_marcher -= 2*(1-dissent); unemployment_insurance_threshold = disfavored; unemployment_insurance_timer = 10; gold_right += 2; ddp_right += 2; ddp_cohesion -= 1; lvp_right += 2; gold_relation -= 6; unionist_relation -= 4; ddp_relation -= 4; lvp_relation -= 4; unemployment_goal_marcher += 1; goal_marcher_cancel_peoples += 1; economic_growth -= 0.2;

We have increased employer contributions to the Poorman's Pension fund, allowing the program to continue without hurting workers and the unemployed. Perhaps understandably, the guild-masters and their political parties are furious, while our base in the Free Guilds and among the unemployed are pleased.

@balance
subtitle: Neither workers nor employers will be entirely satisfied or dissatisfied. [? if in_grand_coalition and ((gold_ideology == "Right") or (gold_ideology == "Moderate" and gold_relation < 40) or (gold_ideology == "Left" and gold_relation < 30)) and not lvp_formed: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> will likely consider the compromise unacceptable. ?][? if in_grand_coalition and ((gold_ideology == "Left" and gold_relation >= 30) or (gold_ideology == "Moderate" and gold_relation >= 40)) and gold_ideology != "Right" and not lvp_formed: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> might grudgingly accept the compromise for now. ?][? if (in_grand_coalition or in_weimar_coalition) and ((lvp_ideology == "Right") or (lvp_ideology == "Moderate" and lvp_relation < 40) or (lvp_ideology == "Left" and lvp_relation < 30)) and lvp_formed: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> will likely consider the compromise unacceptable. ?][? if (in_grand_coalition or in_weimar_coalition) and ((lvp_ideology == "Left" and lvp_relation >= 30) or (lvp_ideology == "Moderate" and lvp_relation >= 40)) and lvp_ideology != "Right" and lvp_formed: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> might grudgingly accept the compromise for now. ?]
on-arrival: commons_marcher -= 4; disfavored_marcher -= 5; commons_collectivist += 3; disfavored_collectivist += 3; disfavored_royalist += 3; left_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 8; center_dissent += 5; welfare -= 1; budget += 1; collectivist_relation -= 4; inflation -= 1; unemployment_insurance_threshold = disfavored; unemployment_insurance_timer = 10; coalition_dissent = 2 if in_grand_coalition and ((gold_ideology == "Right") or (gold_ideology == "Moderate" and gold_relation < 40) or (gold_ideology == "Left" and gold_relation < 30)); coalition_dissent = 2 if (in_grand_coalition or in_weimar_coalition) and ((lvp_ideology == "Right") or (lvp_ideology == "Moderate" and lvp_relation < 40) or (lvp_ideology == "Left" and lvp_relation < 30)) and lvp_formed; coalition_dissent += 1 if in_grand_coalition; coalition_dissent += 1 if (in_weimar_coalition and lvp_formed); gold_right += 1; ddp_right += 1; lvp_right += 1; labor_goal_marcher_peoples += 1; economic_growth -= 0.1;

Neither side is entirely satisfied by our compromise solution. Many of the workers and unemployed see this as a betrayal, although we present it as the successful aversion of a much worse alternative. [? if (in_grand_coalition or (in_weimar_coalition and lvp_formed)): Meanwhile, the [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?] is aghast at the prospect of raising any taxes on businesses at all. ?]